<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48806" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">transgressĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				going across</i>, <i>going over</i>, <i>passing over</i>, <i>passage</i>
			(rare but class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gallorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 33, 81</span></i>
			: tua in Germaniam, Mamert. Pan. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Maxim. 7, 2</span></i>; <i>over
				the sea</i>, <i><span class="en">Gell. 10, 26,
			6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In rhet., i. q. the Gr.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέρβατον,</span>
			<i>transposition</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">transgressio est, quae verborum perturbat
					ordinem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 4, 32, 44</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">transgressio concinna verborum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 3, 54, 207</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 1, 34</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 4, 28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 6,
			66</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A transition</i> in speaking, <i><span class="en">Quint. 4,
				1, 78</span></i>. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>A transgression</i> of the law, Aug. Quaest. in
			Exod. n. 108; <i><span class="en">Ambros. in Luc. 7, §
				164</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
